{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Forty years.</b> Not one of them died under the age of sixty; therefore forty were decreed, so that those who were twenty would reach sixty. The first year was included, even though it preceded the sending of the spies — because from the time they made the calf, this decree arose in thought, except that He waited for them until their measure was filled. And this is what is said: ״וּבְיוֹם פָּקְדִי״ — in the matter of the spies — ״וּפָקַדְתִּי עֲלֵיהֶם חַטָּאתָם״ (Exodus 32). And here too it is said ״תִּשְׂאוּ אֶת עֲוֹנֹתֵיכֶם״ — two iniquities: that of the calf and that of the complaint. And He counted for them in the reckoning of their lives a partial year as a full one; and when they entered the sixtieth year, those who were twenty died." "<b>And you shall bear your harlotries.</b> As the Targum renders: ״וִיקַבְּלוּן יָת חוֹבֵיכוֹן״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:56.660453938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}